[206.642565, "o", "3\t================================================================================\r\n    34\t## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing\r\n    35\t\r\n    36\tExtract policy (authoritative):\r\n    37\t\r\n    38\tThe March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance\r\n    39\tmessages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes\r\n    40\t`sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or\r\n    41\tequal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,\r\n    42\tapply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply\r\n    43\tafter ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.\r\n    44\t\r\n    45\t================================================================================\r\n    46\tBRIEF 4 — ## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence\r\n    47\t================================================================================\r\n    48\t## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice"]
[206.643052, "o", " Precedence\r\n    49\t\r\n    50\tController memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n    51\t\r\n    52\tThe corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several notices\r\n    53\ttarget the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically\r\n    54\tgreatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in\r\n    55\t`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice\r\n    56\tapplies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override\r\n    57\tboth ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.\r\n    58\t\r\n    59\t================================================================================\r\n    60\tBRIEF 5 — ## Investigation Brief 05 — Meeting Amendments and Owners\r\n    61\t================================================================================\r\n    62\tCommittee minutes show owner churn from unsigned drafts. Ledger owner is the\r\n    63\tdefault. Meeting note amendments under `#### Amendment for TXN-<uuid>`"]
[206.643097, "o", " replace\r\n    64\towner when `signed: true` (case insensitive) and, when the amendment includes\r\n    65\t`effective: YYYY-MM-DD`, only if that date is greater than or equal to the\r\n    66\tledger date for the transaction.\r\n    67\t\r\n    68\t================================================================================\r\n    69\tBRIEF 6 — ## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output\r\n    70\t================================================================================\r\n    71\t## Investigation Brief 06 — Effective Dates on Output\r\n    72\t\r\n    73\tAuditor directive (mandatory for extract):\r\n    74\t\r\n    75\tAuditors compared effective_date columns to correction paperwork. Start from the\r\n    76\tledger `date` field (YYYY-MM-DD on output). When a winning correction notice\r\n    77\tsets field `date` or `status`, use that notice's `effective` date as\r\n    78\t`effective_date` only if that correction modified status or date; otherwise\r\n    79\tkeep the ledger date. `amount_usd` is numeric from the ledger with"]
[206.643111, "o", " two decimal\r\n    80\tplaces in CSV and as a JSON number.\r\n    81\t\r\n    82\t================================================================================\r\n    83\tBRIEF 7 — ## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I)\r\n    84\t================================================================================\r\n    85\t## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I)\r\n    86\t\r\n    87\tExtract policy (authoritative):\r\n    88\t\r\n    89\tException coding review: `exception_reason` is null unless a code applies. Set\r\n    90\t`over_limit` when `amount_usd` strictly exceeds 10000. Set `compliance_hold`\r\n    91\twhen final status is `rejected`, a qualifying `compliance@` email referenced\r\n    92\tthat transaction, and that email block includes a `sent:` line. The sent-date\r\n    93\tcomparison used for `compliance_hold` is defined in Investigation Brief 09\r\n    94\t(Mid-Year Amendment), not Brief 03. Multiple reasons join with semicolon in\r\n    95\tlexical order of the reason codes.\r\n    96\t\r\n    97\t=============="]
[206.643123, "o", "==================================================================\r\n    98\tBRIEF 8 — ## Investigation Brief 08 — Exception Flags (Part II) and Artifacts\r\n    99\t================================================================================\r\n   100\t## Investigation Brief 08 — Exception Flags (Part II) and Artifacts\r\n   101\t\r\n   102\tController memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n   103\t\r\n   104\tContinued from Brief 07. Set `policy_waiver` when final status is `approved`,\r\n   105\t`amount_usd` > 10000, and a Policy Exception block exists for that transaction\r\n   106\twith `approved_by: compliance` on its own line. Set `retroactive_review` when\r\n   107\tfinal status is `reversed`, `amount_usd` > 5000, and a winning correction\r\n   108\tnotice changed status for that transaction.\r\n   109\t\r\n   110\t`extract --outdir` must write: `transactions.json` as `{\"items\":[...]}` sorted\r\n   111\tby `transaction_id` ascending with fields transaction_id, owner, status\r\n   112\t(lowercase), effective_date, amount_usd, exception"]
[206.643134, "o", "_reason (null or\r\n   113\tsemicolon-joined codes). `transactions.csv` uses header\r\n   114\ttransaction_id,owner,status,effective_date,amount_usd,exception_reason with the\r\n   115\tsame rows; leave exception_reason blank when null. `exceptions.json` is\r\n   116\t`{\"items\":[...]}` with only rows where exception_reason is set.\r\n   117\t`reconciliation_report.jsonl` is one JSON object per winning correction with\r\n   118\tnotice_id, transaction_id, field, previous_value, new_value, effective, sorted\r\n   119\tby notice_id ascending.\r\n\u001b[?2004hroot@7b07e9f8c4c5:/app# "]
